one of the main item on the agenda of  today's council was enlargement and  stabilisation and association process we  have adopted the presidency statement  that covered turkey Montenegro Serbia  the former yugoslav republic of  macedonia albania bosnia herzegovina and  kosovo and let me say quite frankly that  we wanted to achieve more we wanted to  have counsel conclusions however one  country was unable to support the  compromise which all remaining 27 member  states found acceptable when put on the  table we welcome the new approach to  address the fundamental reforms early in  the process especially when it comes to  the rule of law and fundamental rights  it's clear to understand that the  enlargement process is not about giving  gifts to the participating countries but  it's really about hard and credible work  that benefits both sides the council  formally adopted its negotiating  position on the european fund for  sustainable development and this is an  important milestone in our efforts to  make this fund a reality this fund is a  vital instrument which aims in  particular at tackling the root causes  of irregular migration by creating job  opportunities encouraging investments  and facilitating sustainable  developments in partner countries in  africa as well as in the european  union's neighborhood we have approved  the joint declaration setting out the  eels priorities for the year 2017 as  agreed by the silver presidency with the  European Commission and the European  Parliament this is the first time that  the three EU institutions agree on a  legislative priorities for the following  year
 

